    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T04:20:34Z",
    "body": "Correction (M3, who filed this): there is no defect. Setup order is name order (`setup::setups` reads `model::named_entities`, sorted by name), so a setup that undo re-creates sorts back into its old place. #1361's test created \"Front\" then \"Back\" and saw [\"Back\", \"Front\"], which is name order and was already the order before the delete. I've moved this from P3 bug to P7 (a missing pin). PR #1364 adds that pin: delete a middle setup, undo, and the posted program is byte-identical.",
